<title>USA: Northeast Indiana Bancorp completes stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Northeast Indiana Bancorp completes stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>HUFFINGTON, Ind. 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Indiana Bancorp Inc said Wednesday it completed its fourth stock repurchase program, originally launched in September.</p>
<p>The company said it bought back nearly 197,000 common shares, representing about 10 percent of its stock, at an average price of $13.47 a share. The bank holding company said it now has about 1.8 million shares in public hands.</p>
<p>Some of the shares will fund its employee incentive plan, the company said.</p>
<p>Northeast Indiana Bancorp shares were unchanged Wednesday at 15-3/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
